Question 14: Reshape np.arange(1, 13) into (3, 4), (2, 6), (2, 3, 2) and (4, -1). Print the shape of each.

AIM: Understanding usage of array.reshape() function

Code:
import numpy as np
a=np.arange(1, 13)
print(a.reshape(3,4).shape)
print(a.reshape(2,6).shape)
print(a.reshape(2,3,2).shape)
print(a.reshape(4,-1).shape)

Output:
(3, 4)
(2, 6)
(2, 3, 2)
(4, 3)

Explanation:
Functions used: array.reshape(), array.shape()
Usage: array.reshape() changes the shape(dimensions) of array as specified.
array.shape() returns the shape(dimensions) of the array
